      {/* Section 5: Scooter Safety */}
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 sm:mb-8">
          5. Scooter Safety Card
        </h2>

        <div class="prose prose-sm sm:prose max-w-none space-y-6">
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            1-page printable: pre-rental inspection (10 items), road rules, police bribe reality, emergency contacts, insurance.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border-l-4 border-red-400 p-4 sm:p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">Pre-Rental Inspection Checklist</h3>
            <ol class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700">
              <li>[ ] <strong>Brakes:</strong> Front + rear responsive. Squeeze brake handle; should feel firm.</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Tires:</strong> Tread visible. Not bald. Check both.</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Lights:</strong> Front + rear light work. Headlight is critical.</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Horn:</strong> Loud. Test it.</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Engine:</strong> Starts easily, no rough idle. Ask them to rev it.</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Fuel:</strong> Tank is full or nearly full (record fuel level).</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Body/mirrors:</strong> No major damage. Take photos of existing scratches.</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Lock/key:</strong> Lock works smoothly. Key doesn't stick.</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Registration + documents:</strong> Rental shop should have paperwork. Take photo of it.</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Insurance:</strong> Ask "berapa asuransi?" (how much insurance?). Pay IDR 50–100k extra for coverage.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-yellow-50 rounded-lg p-4 sm:p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">Road Rules (you need to know)</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700">
              <li><strong>Drive LEFT side of road.</strong> (Yes, Bali drives on the left.)</li>
              <li><strong>Helmet required.</strong> Police WILL stop you without one. Fines IDR 100k ($6).</li>
              <li><strong>Speed limits:</strong> 60 km/h in towns, 80 km/h on highways. Enforce loosely but don't push it.</li>
              <li><strong>Lights on:</strong> Even during day, headlight on = safer + legally required.</li>
              <li><strong>No mobile phones.</strong> Using phone while riding = IDR 100k fine.</li>
              <li><strong>Horn before passing.</strong> Drivers here EXPECT honking. Honk = "I'm coming around."</li>
              <li><strong>Stop at red lights.</strong> Locals run them but foreigners can't. Police target tourists.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-4 sm:p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">Police Bribe Reality Check</h3>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700 mb-3">
              <strong>Common story:</strong> "Police stopped me and asked for a 'donation.'"
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700 mb-3">
              <strong>What's real:</strong> Police CAN stop tourists. Fines are legit (IDR 100–500k depending on violation). They may informally offer to "settle it here" = bribe. It's technically illegal but happens.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700">
              <strong>How to handle:</strong> Ask for a receipt ("kuitansi?"). Most will give formal receipt instead of taking bribe. If they insist on bribe, negotiate down (IDR 100k typical) and move on. IMPORTANT: If you have international license + rental papers, most police let you go.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">Common Road Hazards</h3>
            <table class="w-full text-sm sm:text-base border-collapse">
              <thead>
                <tr class="bg-gray-200">
                  <th class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2 text-left font-bold">Hazard</th>
                  <th class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2 text-left font-bold">How to Avoid</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2"><strong>Potholes / uneven road</strong></td>
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2">Scan road ahead. Slow down in wet season.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2"><strong>Stray dogs / dogs crossing</strong></td>
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2">Honk early. Slow down. Most move out of way.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2"><strong>Scooter / motorbike coming at you (wrong side)</strong></td>
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2">Expect it. Move right, brake, let them pass. Happens daily.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2"><strong>Rain = slippery roads</strong></td>
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2">Slow down 30%. Don't brake hard. Avoid rainy season riding if possible.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2"><strong>Traffic jams (esp. Canggu)</strong></td>
                  <td class="border border-gray-300 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2">Leave early. Avoid 7–9 AM + 5–7 PM rush hours.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border-l-4 border-red-400 p-4 sm:p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">When NOT to Ride</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700">
              <li>[ ] After drinking (accidents are common, police check)</li>
              <li>[ ] At night if you don't know the road (headlights can be dodgy)</li>
              <li>[ ] During heavy rain (visibility + traction are terrible)</li>
              <li>[ ] If you're not confident (best to use Grab instead)</li>
              <li>[ ] On highways / main roads without experience</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">Insurance + Documents</h3>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700 mb-3">
              <strong>Always get insurance:</strong> IDR 50–100k ($3–6) covers basic damage. Ask rental shop for detailed policy.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700 mb-3">
              <strong>Bring:</strong> International driving license (IDP) from your home country. Passport. Rental agreement (photo copy).
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700">
              <strong>If accident:</strong> Call police (call 110 or ask bystander). Get police report number. Report to rental shop IMMEDIATELY. Be honest — most insurance is basic and covers damage up to IDR 5M.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

