      {/* Section 10: Rainy Season */}
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 sm:mb-8">
          10. Rainy Season Survival Kit
        </h2>

        <div class="prose prose-sm sm:prose max-w-none space-y-6">
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Packing checklist (8 essentials), 10 indoor activities by area, monthly rain intensity calendar, timing guide for activities.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-blue-50 rounded-lg p-4 sm:p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">Rainy Season Overview (Nov–March)</h3>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700 mb-3">
              <strong>What it means:</strong> Not continuous rain. Usually 1–3 hours per day, often afternoon/evening. Mornings often clear + beautiful. High humidity (80–90%).
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700">
              <strong>Upside:</strong> 30–50% cheaper accommodation. Fewer tourists. Flights cheaper. <strong>Downside:</strong> Humidity. Potential delays. Scooters riskier.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">Packing Checklist (8 Essentials)</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700">
              <li>[ ] <strong>Lightweight rain jacket</strong> (compact, packable, quick-dry)</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Quick-dry pants / shorts</strong> (NOT jeans; polyester/nylon dries in 2–3 hours)</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Waterproof bag</strong> (for phone, documents, valuables)</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Umbrella or rain cap</strong> (compact umbrella + rain cap = backup options)</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Fast-drying shoes</strong> (trainers or waterproof hiking shoes, NOT canvas)</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Moisture-absorbing products</strong> (silica gel packs for electronics, clothes)</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Compact towel</strong> (microfiber, quick-dry, doesn't mold)</li>
              <li>[ ] <strong>Fungal cream</strong> (Lotrimin or generic; humidity = higher fungal infection risk)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

