            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Examples:</strong> Ubud: Palace + Museum, Cooking class, Art workshop, Yoga drop-in, Market crawl. Canggu: Coworking day-pass, Spa treatment, Fitness class, Café crawl, Live music.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-4 sm:p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-base sm:text-lg">Rainy-Season Hacks</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700">
              <li><strong>Weather:</strong> Check Google Maps weather hourly (real-time in Bali).</li>
              <li><strong>Plan 2 activities/day:</strong> One outdoor (morning), one indoor (afternoon backup).</li>
              <li><strong>Scooter:</strong> Ride only in dry conditions. If rain starts, grab a café or Grab ride.</li>
              <li><strong>Health:</strong> Change clothes if soaked (prevents fungal). Hang clothes outside after rain. Shower daily. Drink extra water.</li>
              <li><strong>Social:</strong> Join coworking communities. Yoga + wellness events MORE in rainy season. Cooking + art classes cheaper + less crowded.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border-l-4 border-red-400 p-4 sm:p-6">
